---
import AppLandingPage from '../../components/AppLandingPage.astro';
import { appsForLicense } from '../../data/apps';
import { priceText } from '../../data/stores';

const apps = appsForLicense('sbf-see');

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Which app is best for SBF See?',
    a: 'If you do not want to pay: Sportbootführerschein See 2023 by Matthias Wimmer – completely free, no ads, but without the navigation tasks. If you want to practise the navigation tasks thoroughly on an iPhone: SBF See by Ralf Goritz. If you want explanations for each answer and a companion online course: Bootspruefung.de. If you are combining SBF See with other licences and do not want a subscription: Boatpass.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do the apps cover the navigation tasks?',
    a: 'Not all of them. Besides the multiple-choice questions, the SBF See exam includes a navigation section with chartwork, course calculation and position fixing. The free Wimmer app does not cover it. Boatpass, Bootspruefung.de, Bootsprüfung, SBF-Fragen and SBF See by Ralf Goritz do. A printed exercise set with the official practice chart is still worth having – in the exam you work on paper.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How many questions does the SBF See exam have?',
    a: 'The official SBF See catalogue holds 285 questions (72 basic and 213 coastal questions) plus 15 navigation tasks. The exam paper contains 30 questions: 7 basic and 23 coastal-specific ones, plus one navigation task.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is an app enough to pass SBF See?',
    a: 'For the theory, yes, provided you work through the whole catalogue and practise the navigation tasks separately. The practical exam – manoeuvres and knots – can only be learned on the water.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is there an SBF See app for iPhone?',
    a: 'Yes, several in fact: Bootspruefung.de, Bootsprüfung, Bootsschule1, SBF-Fragen, Sailbyte, Boatpass (since October 2026) and SBF See by Ralf Goritz, which is available for iOS only. Only the free Wimmer app is limited to Android.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do the apps work offline?',
    a: 'Boatpass, SBF-Fragen, Bootsprüfung, SBF See by Ralf Goritz and the Wimmer app work offline. With Bootspruefung.de, full offline use is part of the Pro version. With Sailbyte, SBF See and Binnen are usable offline.',
  },
];

const relatedLinks = [
  { href: '/en/sbf-coastal/', label: 'SBF See – exam, costs and procedure' },
  { href: '/en/sbf-coastal-exam-questions/', label: 'SBF See exam questions explained' },
  { href: '/en/sbf-app/', label: 'All boating licence apps compared' },
  { href: '/en/sbf-inland-app/', label: 'SBF Binnen apps compared' },
  { href: '/en/sbf-coastal-navigation-tasks/', label: 'SBF Coastal navigation tasks step by step' },
  { href: '/en/blog/sbf-coastal-navigation-tasks-explained/', label: 'SBF See navigation tasks explained' },
  { href: '/en/blog/sbf-inland-vs-coastal/', label: 'SBF Binnen or See – which licence fits?' },
];
---

<AppLandingPage
  lang="en"
  title="SBF Coastal App: the best apps compared 2026"
  description="Looking for an SBF See app? Eight Android and iPhone apps compared on price, ratings and who really covers the navigation tasks – including Boatpass."
  altUrl="https://boatpass.de/sbf-see-app/"
  path="/sbf-coastal-app/"
  breadcrumbName="SBF See apps compared"
  badge="Sportbootführerschein See"
  h1="SBF See apps compared"
  heroIntro="Eight apps cover the official SBF See question catalogue – at very different prices and with very different depth on the navigation tasks. Here they are side by side."
  answer="Eight widely used learning apps are worth considering for SBF See. Free and highly rated is Sportbootführerschein See 2023 by Matthias Wimmer, but it does not cover the navigation tasks. The most ratings go to Bootspruefung.de and SBF See by Ralf Goritz (iOS only, with animated navigation tasks). Bootsprüfung, SBF-Fragen and Boatpass also include chartwork, Sailbyte runs on a monthly subscription, and Bootsschule1 belongs to a complete course."
  apps={apps}
  tableCaption="Every app covering the official SBF See question catalogue – sorted alphabetically."
  androidHeading="SBF See app for Android"
  androidParagraphs={[
    'Apart from SBF See by Ralf Goritz, all the apps are on Google Play. The most widely used free option is <strong>Sportbootführerschein See 2023</strong> by Matthias Wimmer, with over 100,000 downloads – no ads, no in-app purchases, no tracking. It works on a spaced-repetition principle: a question counts as done only once you have answered it correctly five times.',
    'The decisive catch: it <strong>does not cover the navigation tasks</strong>. For course calculation, dead reckoning and chartwork you need extra material – or an app that includes that part.',
    'Boatpass is on Google Play too. The SBF See catalogue costs ' + priceText('sbfSee', 'en') + ' as a one-off, or ' + priceText('bundleSbf', 'en') + ' bundled with SBF Binnen. Trying the app is free.',
  ]}
  iosHeading="SBF See app for iPhone and iPad"
  iosParagraphs={[
    'On iPhone the choice is wide. <strong>SBF See by Ralf Goritz</strong> deserves a special mention: it is available for iOS only, it is the most-rated coastal-only app, and it shows every navigation task as an animation for paper and digital charts. Alongside it, <strong>Bootspruefung.de</strong>, <strong>SBF-Fragen</strong>, <strong>Bootsprüfung</strong>, <strong>Bootsschule1</strong>, <strong>Sailbyte</strong> and <strong>Boatpass</strong> are on the App Store.',
    'The free Wimmer app is not in the App Store. <strong>Boatpass has been available there since October 2026</strong>; a purchase only applies to the store you bought in, so an Android purchase does not unlock anything on iPhone.',
  ]}
  strengths={[
    'Complete official SBF See catalogue including navigation tasks',
    'Exam simulation with pass mark and time limit',
    'Mistake training for the questions you answered wrongly',
    'Combinable with SBF Binnen, UBI, SRC and LRC in the same app',
    '€9.99 one-off for the SBF See catalogue, no subscription',
    'Study offline – works without an internet connection',
  ]}
  limitations={[
    'Purchases apply per store – no transfer between Android and iPhone',
    'No SKS – anyone continuing to the coastal skipper licence needs a second app',
    'Still few ratings compared with Bootspruefung.de, Goritz or Wimmer',
    'No companion online course in the browser',
    'Does not replace practical training or practising on the paper chart',
  ]}
  faqs={faqs}
  relatedLinks={relatedLinks}
>
  <section slot="after-table" style="margin-bottom:48px;">
    <h2 class="content-section-title" style="margin-bottom:16px;">Navigation tasks: what the apps cover</h2>
    <p style="font-size:16px; color:#4B5563; line-height:1.75; margin-bottom:12px;">
      The navigation section is what sets SBF See apart from the inland licence: 15 official tasks with course calculation, bearings and position fixing on practice chart D49. In the exam you solve one of them on paper, with navigation instruments. The apps handle this very differently (according to store descriptions and vendor websites, as of October 2026):
    </p>
    <p style="font-size:16px; color:#4B5563; line-height:1.75; margin-bottom:12px;">
      <strong>SBF See by Ralf Goritz</strong> shows every navigation task as an animation, for paper and digital charts, and includes practice chart D49 in digital form. <strong>Bootspruefung.de</strong> explains the tasks in its video course. <strong>Bootsprüfung</strong>, <strong>SBF-Fragen</strong> and <strong>Boatpass</strong> include the navigation tasks; Boatpass tests each task in nine sub-questions. The free <strong>Wimmer app</strong> contains no navigation tasks.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size:16px; color:#4B5563; line-height:1.75; margin-bottom:12px;">
      Whichever app you use, work through at least a few tasks on the printed chart, because there is no screen in the exam. The solution for each task type is on the page <a href="/en/sbf-coastal-navigation-tasks/" style="color:#3366FF; text-decoration:underline;">SBF Coastal navigation tasks step by step</a>. We explain how the tasks are structured in the article <a href="/en/blog/sbf-coastal-navigation-tasks-explained/" style="color:#3366FF; text-decoration:underline;">SBF See navigation tasks explained</a>, and course conversion in the article <a href="/en/blog/course-conversion-sbf-coastal/" style="color:#3366FF; text-decoration:underline;">Course conversion for SBF See</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</AppLandingPage>
